{
  "preset_id": "linkedin_video_ads",
  "platform": "LinkedIn",
  "display_name": "LinkedIn — Video Ads",
  "description": "Sponsored in-feed video ads. MP4 only, tightly bounded dimensions, and a published 5% aspect-ratio tolerance.",
  "origin": "shipped",
  "ruleset_version": "2026-08-09.1",
  "last_verified_date": "2026-08-09",
  "byte_convention": "Decimal bytes (500 MB = 500,000,000; the 75 KB floor is treated as 76,800 bytes). LinkedIn does not state binary or decimal, so PreflightQC uses the conservative reading.",
  "caveats": [
    "The maximum ad file size is 500 MB, per LinkedIn's own specification page and the Microsoft Learn Videos API. The 200 MB figure repeated in many third-party blogs is not authoritative and is not used here.",
    "LinkedIn publishes an explicit 5% aspect-ratio tolerance, which PreflightQC applies to the ratio bounds.",
    "LinkedIn does not publish a hard video-codec whitelist for ads, so non-H.264 is a warning rather than a failure. Apple ProRes is separately documented as unsupported and does fail.",
    "Captions are supplied as a separate SRT sidecar or burned into the picture. Neither is determinable from the delivered file, so caption presence is never checked.",
    "Organic and advertising specifications are different products and must never be merged."
  ],
  "sources": [
